my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
line one
line two
line three
line four
line five
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{Multiple marks (a, b) coexist and can be jumped between},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/mark_multiple`

Multiple marks can be set and jumped between independently. **ma** and **mb** store separate positions; `` `a `` and `` `b `` jump to their respective locations.

**Keys:** `ma` then `jj` then `mb` then `j` then `` `a `` then `` `b ``

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0

**after_mark_a.png**
- Mark 'a' set at line 1, col 0
- Cursor still at line 1

**after_mark_b.png**
- Moved down 2 lines to line 3, col 0
- Mark 'b' set at line 3, col 0

**after_move_down.png**
- Cursor at line 4, col 0

**after_jump_a.png**
- Cursor back at line 1, col 0 (mark 'a' location)

**after_jump_b.png**
- Cursor at line 3, col 0 (mark 'b' location)
- Both marks preserved independently
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ma');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_mark_a');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('jj');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('mb');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_mark_b');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('j');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_down');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('`a');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_jump_a');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('`b');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_jump_b');
    },
}
